				<coordinates>-139.4355728408225,64.07082889448039,0</coordinates>
			</Point>
		</Placemark>
		<Placemark>
			<name>Stewart, BC (Canada) and Hyder, Alaska</name>
			<description>We had a delightful couple of days exploring the glaciers and the bears in this area - and then Nancy somehow arranged for the US Post Office mail plane (a little float plane) to take us and our bikes over the mountains and Misty Fjords National Monument into Ketchikan, Alaska.</description>
			<LookAt>
				<longitude>-130.02804</longitude>
				<latitude>55.9147</latitude>
				<altitude>0</altitude>
				<heading>2.073804698175827e-14</heading>
				<tilt>0</tilt>
				<range>19592.55532429537</range>
			</LookAt>
			<styleUrl>#msn_airports</styleUrl>
			<Point>
				<coordinates>-130.02804,55.9147,0</coordinates>
			</Point>
		</Placemark>
		<Placemark>
			<name>Ketchikan</name>
			<description>Ketchikan is a major center of Native American culture, with some pretty amazing Totems, and we enjoyed all that the and temperate rain forests that result from the 24x7 rain... Then we took the ferry to Prince Rupert, BC.</description>
